            "_comment": "T-708 (2026-08-04, supersedes the T-660 SOLO+DUO triple): three spawns could not feed the ~15 wolf kills the starter quest set demands (q001 8+~3-for-pelts, q010 3, q004 1), and the fun-audit re-flagged the (30,20)/(36,24) duo as the #52 chain-pull \u2014 a 2v1 against a fresh L1 following Kessa's very first real-mob quest. The starter band is now SIX ALL-SOLO spawns ringing the hamlet ((30,20) kept for the test-loot-loop 1101 fixture; (36,24) and (20,-30) relocated; three added on the far/west+south sides), every pair >=30m apart \u2014 T-708 asked >=15m, but 15-30m is exactly T-402's 8-30m dead zone, so the solo floor (1.5x AGGRO_MAX) is the honest spacing \u2014 and EVERY spawn >=30m from every spawn_points.json hub (the T-515 invariant extended to the L3 starter wolves now that respawn is fast: worst case 20m aggro + 6m hub jitter = 26m). Also kept: >=20m from every elite (T-617 escape buffer: Greymaw (48,40), Grexrok (-45,42), Elderthorn (-50,-45)), >=30m from the kobold/lasher camps (no cross-family chain), >=18m (wolf leash_radius) from every trainer/service NPC per test_trainer_spawn_safety.gd, and clear of the lake disc (18,22 r12). respawn_ticks 300 = ~15s at 20tps (starter-band only; the global 600 dwell stands elsewhere) so two simultaneous newcomers each sustain kill progress without >20s of no-target downtime. Spacing regression: test_spawn_safety.gd (starter-wolf density test) + test_spawn_spacing.gd's Wold dead-zone lint (starter solos; the heartwold duos still provide the cluster vocabulary).",
