        {
            "_pull_vocabulary_doc": "T-402 Ashmoor street-tier PULL VOCABULARY \u2014 the encounter grammar the T-399 live E2E lacked and the M6 crypt content reuses. Under the T-402 level-relative aggro model (mob_aggro.gd) these street mobs aggro at their WoW-shape base reach (~16-18m same-level, capped AGGRO_MAX=20), so spacing \u2014 not a near-contact radius \u2014 is what makes a pull SOLO, DUO, or PACK. THREE deliberate shapes: (a) SOLO = a lone mob whose nearest neighbour is >= 1.5*AGGRO_MAX (30m) away, so it can be engaged 1v1 (the T-399 winnable fight, unreachable before because every legbreaker had a constable ~5m off forcing a 2v1); (b) DUO/PACK = a cluster whose members sit <= 8m apart (they read as standing TOGETHER and are pulled as one honest group), the cluster itself >= 30m from every other group. The forbidden DEAD ZONE is 8-30m: two mobs that close chain by accident yet look separate \u2014 exactly the 4.9m legbreaker+constable trap. test_spawn_spacing.gd ASSERTS every Ashmoor pair is <=8m (same group) OR >=30m (separate pull); it fails CLOSED so future authoring can't silently recreate the trap. Every spawn is also >= AGGRO_MAX+margin from the ASHMOOR_ARRIVAL plaza (-420,-5) so a fresh rift arrival (possibly UNDER-level -> aggro grows toward the cap) is not swarmed on step-in (T-330 vestibule lesson). T-618 (2026-07-19): SOLO-A also has to clear the High Street SERVICE ROW (constabulary/Grey Gull/warehouse anchors at y=8, x -428.5..-412.75) by its own leash_radius (20m, live-proven: a L3 pilot was killed 14-16m off the row by the original (-420,22) spawn) \u2014 moved north to (-420,29), which is the only y on this x column that clears BOTH the row (>=20m, its true worst-case reach) AND PACK-D's dead zone (>=30m, nearest member is a gunsel at (-422,60)) simultaneously; see test_spawn_spacing.gd's service-hub exclusion test. GROUPS: SOLO-A legbreaker (-420,29); SOLO-B constable (-458,42); DUO-C legbreaker+constable (~-382,49); PACK-D seance_warden + gunsel x2 + torpedo (~-425,62) \u2014 the ranged hard pull.",
